---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy"
  description="Visitor statistics, cookies and embedded content on Notes Along the Way."
>
  <article class="reading">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This website is published by Danilo Poccia. You can read it without
        accepting optional analytics.
      </p>
      <h2>Visitor statistics</h2>
      <p>
        When enabled, optional analytics use PostHog Cloud EU (Frankfurt) to
        understand visits, approximate reading engagement, collection
        navigation, code-copy actions, viewer openings, simulator starts and
        book-download clicks.
      </p>
      <p>
        Analytics start only after you choose Accept analytics. PostHog uses a
        first-party cookie with a pseudonymous browser identifier to estimate
        repeat visits. It receives the page path, referring domain,
        browser/device details and the selected action. Your connection also
        exposes your IP address to the service, which may be used for
        approximate location. We do not send URL query strings, fragment text,
        form contents, code contents or AI prompts. Session recordings and
        automatic interaction recording are disabled.
      </p>
      <p>
        We remember your choice in this browser for up to 180 days using local
        storage. Analytics cookies expire after up to 180 days without renewal.
        Event retention is up to one year under the configured free plan. No
        separate export archive is currently configured. Refusing analytics does
        not prevent access to content.
      </p>
      <p>
        Use Privacy settings in the footer whenever analytics are enabled to
        change your choice. Withdrawal stops future collection and clears the
        analytics identifier on this browser; it does not automatically delete
        previously collected events.
      </p>
      <p>
        Read <a href="https://posthog.com/privacy">PostHog’s privacy policy</a>{" "}
        for details of the service and its processing.
      </p>
      <h2>Embedded content</h2>
      <p>
        External viewers load when you choose Load viewer. The external provider
        then receives your connection and may apply its own privacy and cookie
        policies. Analytics consent is separate. You can use the ordinary
        external link instead. Reading inside external documents or videos is
        not measured unless a supported integration is explicitly added.
      </p>
      <h2>Hosting and questions</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted with AWS Amplify. Hosting services process technical
        requests to deliver and protect the site; optional analytics controls do
        not disable those essential requests.
      </p>
      <p>
        For privacy questions or data requests, contact Danilo through the
        profiles on the <a href="/about/">About page</a>. Analytics identifiers
        are not linked to a login or your name, so locating a particular
        visitor’s historic events may require additional information.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
